{
  "title": "68: Al-Qalam القلم",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللَّهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nنٓ وَالْقَلَمِ وَمَا يَسْطُرُونَ (1)\nNOOON, WAL QALAME WA MAA YASTOROON.\nNun. By the Pen and what they write:\nمَآ اَنتَ بِنِعْمَةِ رَبِّكَ بِمَجْنُونٍ (2)\nMAA ANTA BE-NE’MATE RABBEKA BE-MAJNOON.\nby your Lord’s blessing, you are not, crazy,\nوَاِنَّ لَكَ لَاَجْرًا غَيْرَ مَمْنُونٍ (3)\nWA INNA LAKA LA-AJRAN GHAYRA MAMNOON.\nand yours indeed will be an everlasting reward,\nوَاِنَّكَ لَعَلَىٰ خُلُقٍ عَظِيمٍ (4)\nWA INNAKA LA-A’LAA KHOLOQIN A’ZEEM.\nand indeed you possess a great character.\nفَسَتُبْصِرُ وَيُبْصِرُونَ (5)\nFASATUBSERO WA YUBSEROON.\nYou will see and they will see,\nبِاَييِّكُمُ الْمَفْتُونُ (6)\nBE-AYYEKOMUL MAFTOON.\nwhich one of you is crazy.\nاِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِمَن ضَلَّ عَن سَبِيلِهِۦ وَهُوَ اَعْلَمُ بِالْمُهْتَدِينَ (7)\nINNA RABBAKA HOWA A-A’LAMO BEMAN ZALLA A’N SABEELEHI WA HOWA A-A’LAMO BIL-MOHTADEEN.\nIndeed your Lord knows best those who stray from His way, and He knows best those who are guided.\nفَلَا تُطِعِ الْمُكَذِّبِينَ (8)\nFALAA TOTE-I’L MOKAZZEBEEN.\nSo do not obey the deniers,\nوَدُّوا۟ لَوْ تُدْهِنُ فَيُدْهِنُونَ (9)\nWADDOO LAW TUDHENO FA-YUDHENOON.\nwho are eager that you should be flexible, so that they [too] may be flexible [towards you].\nوَلَا تُطِعْ كُلَّ حَلَّافٍ مَّهِينٍ (10)\nWA LAA TOTE’ KULLA HALLAAFIM MAHEEN.\nAnd do not obey any vile swearer,\nهَمَّازٍ مَّشَّآءٍۭ بِنَمِيمٍ (11)\nHAMMAAZIM MASH-SHAAA-IM BE-NAMEEM.\nscandal-monger, talebearer,\nمَّنَّاعٍ لِّلْخَيْرِ مُعْتَدٍ اَثِيمٍ (12)\nMANNAA-I’L LIL-KHAYRE MO’TADIN ASEEM.\nhinderer of all good, sinful transgressor,\nعُتُلٍّۭ بَعْدَ ذٰلِكَ زَنِيمٍ (13)\nO’TULLIM BA’DA ZAALEKA ZANEEM.\ncallous and, on top of that, baseborn\nاَن كَانَ ذَا مَالٍ وَبَنِينَ (14)\nAN KAANA ZAA MAALINW WA BANEEN.\n—[who behaves in such a manner only] because he has wealth and children.\nاِذَا تُتْلَىٰ عَلَيْهِ ءَايٰتُنَا قَالَ اَسٰطِيرُ الْاَوَّلِينَ (15)\nEZAA TUTLAA A’LAYHE AAYAATONAA QAALA ASAATEERUL AWWALEEN.\nWhen Our signs are recited to him, he says, ‘Myths of the ancients!’\nسَنَسِمُهُۥ عَلَى الْخُرْطُومِ (16)\nSANASEMOHU A’LAL KHURTOOM.\nSoon We shall brand him on his snout.\nاِنَّا بَلَوْنٰهُمْ كَمَا بَلَوْنَآ اَصْحٰبَ الْجَنَّةِ اِذْ اَقْسَمُوا۟ لَيَصْرِمُنَّهَا مُصْبِحِينَ (17)\nINNAA BALAWNAAHUM KAMAA BALAWNAA ASHAABAL JANNATE IZ AQSAMOO LAYASREMUNNAHAA MUSBEHEEN.\nIndeed we have tested them just as We tested the People of the Garden when they vowed they would gather its fruit at dawn,\nوَلَا يَسْتَثْنُونَ (18)\nWA LAA YASTASNOON.\nand they did not make any exception.\nفَطَافَ عَلَيْهَا طَآئِفٌ مِّن رَّبِّكَ وَهُمْ نَآئِمُونَ (19)\nFA-TAAFA A’LAYHAA TAAA-EFUM MIR RABBEKA WA HUM NAAA-EMOON.\nThen, a visitation from your Lord visited it while they were asleep.\nفَاَصْبَحَتْ كَالصَّرِيمِ (20)\nFA-ASBAHAT KAS-SAREEM.\nSo, by dawn it was like a harvested field.\nفَتَنَادَوْا۟ مُصْبِحِينَ (21)\nFA-TANAADAW MUSBEHEEN.\nAt dawn they called out to one another,\nاَنِ اغْدُوا۟ عَلَىٰ حَرْثِكُمْ اِن كُنتُمْ صٰرِمِينَ (22)\nANIGH DOO A’LAA HARSEKUM IN KUNTUM SAAREMEEN.\n‘Get off early to your field if you have to gather [the fruits].’\nفَانطَلَقُوا۟ وَهُمْ يَتَخٰفَتُونَ (23)\nFANTALAQOO WA HUM YATAKHAAFATOON.\nSo off they went, murmuring to one another:\nاَن لَّا يَدْخُلَنَّهَا الْيَوْمَ عَلَيْكُم مِّسْكِينٌ (24)\nAL LAA YADKHOLANNAHAL YAWMA A’LAYKUM MISKEEN.\n‘Today no needy man shall come to you in it.’\nوَغَدَوْا۟ عَلَىٰ حَرْدٍ قٰدِرِينَ (25)\nWA GHADAW A’LAA HARDIN QAADEREEN.\nAnd they set out at early morning, [considering themselves] able to deprive [the poor of its fruit].\nفَلَمَّا رَاَوْهَا قَالُوٓا۟ اِنَّا لَضَآلُّونَ (26)\nFALAMMAA RA-AWHAA QAALOO INNAA LA-ZAALLOON.\nBut when they saw it, they said, ‘We have indeed lost our way!’\nبَلْ نَحْنُ مَحْرُومُونَ (27)\nBAL NAHNO MAHROOMOON.\n‘No, it is we who have been deprived!’\nقَالَ اَوْسَطُهُمْ اَلَمْ اَقُل لَّكُمْ لَوْلَا تُسَبِّحُونَ (28)\nQAALA AWSATOHUM ALAM AQUL LAKUM LAWLAA TOSABBEHOON.\nThe most upright among them said, ‘Did I not tell you, ‘‘Why do you not glorify [Allah]?’’ ’\nقَالُوا۟ سُبْحٰنَ رَبِّنَآ اِنَّا كُنَّا ظٰلِمِينَ (29)\nQAALOO SUBHAANA RABBENAA INNAA KUNNAA ZAALEMEEN.\nThey said, ‘Immaculate is our Lord! We have indeed been wrongdoers!’\nفَاَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَعْضٍ يَتَلٰوَمُونَ (30)\nFA-AQBALA BA’ZOHUM A’LAA BA’ZIN-Y YATALAAWAMOON.\nThen they turned to one another, blaming each other.\nقَالُوا۟ يٰوَيْلَنَآ اِنَّا كُنَّا طٰغِينَ (31)\nQAALOO YAA WAYLANAA INNAA KUNNAA TAAGHEEN.\nThey said, ‘Woe to us! Indeed, we have been rebellious.\nعَسَىٰ رَبُّنَآ اَن يُبْدِلَنَا خَيْرًا مِّنْهَآ اِنَّآ اِلَىٰ رَبِّنَا رٰغِبُونَ (32)\nA’SAA RABBONAA AN-Y YUBDELANAA KHAYRAM MINHAA INNAA ELAA RABBENAA RAAGHEBOON.\nMaybe our Lord will give us a better one in its place. Indeed we earnestly beseech our Lord.’\nكَذٰلِكَ الْعَذَابُ وَلَعَذَابُ الْءَاخِرَةِ اَكْبَرُ لَوْ كَانُوا۟ يَعْلَمُونَ (33)\nKAZAALEKAL A’ZAAB, WA LA-A’ZAABUL AAKHERATE AKBAR, LAW KAANOO YA’LAMOON.\nSuch was their punishment; and the punishment of the Hereafter is surely greater, had they known.\nاِنَّ لِلْمُتَّقِينَ عِندَ رَبِّهِمْ جَنّٰتِ النَّعِيمِ (34)\nINNA LIL-MUTTAQEENA I’NDA RABBEHIM JANNAATIN NA-E’EM.\nIndeed for the Godwary there will be gardens of bliss near their Lord.\nاَفَنَجْعَلُ الْمُسْلِمِينَ كَالْمُجْرِمِينَ (35)\nAFA-NAJ-A’LUL MUSLEMEENA KAL-MUJREMEEN.\nShall We treat those who submit [to Us] as [We treat] the guilty?\nمَا لَكُمْ كَيْفَ تَحْكُمُونَ (36)\nMAA LAKUM KAYFA TAHKOMOON.\nWhat is the matter with you? How do you judge!\nاَمْ لَكُمْ كِتٰبٌ فِيهِ تَدْرُسُونَ (37)\nAM LAKUM KETAABUN FEEHE TADROSOON.\nDo you possess a scripture in which you read\nاِنَّ لَكُمْ فِيهِ لَمَا تَخَيَّرُونَ (38)\nINNA LAKUM FEEHE LAMAA TAKHAYYAROON.\nthat you shall have in it whatever you choose?\nاَمْ لَكُمْ اَيْمٰنٌ عَلَيْنَا بٰلِغَةٌ اِلَىٰ يَوْمِ الْقِيٰمَةِ اِنَّ لَكُمْ لَمَا تَحْكُمُونَ (39)\nAM LAKUM AYMAANUN A’LAYNAA BAALEGHATUN ELAA YAWMIL QEYAAMATE, INNA LAKUM LAMAA TAHKOMOON.\nDo you have a pledge binding on Us until the Day of Resurrection, that you shall indeed have whatever you decide?\nسَلْهُمْ اَيُّهُم بِذٰلِكَ زَعِيمٌ (40)\nSALHUM AYYOHUM BEZAALEKA ZA-E’EM.\nAsk them, which of them will aver [any of] that!\nاَمْ لَهُمْ شُرَكَآءُ فَلْيَاْتُوا۟ بِشُرَكَآئِهِمْ اِن كَانُوا۟ صٰدِقِينَ (41)\nAM LAHUM SHORAKAAA-O FALYAATOO BE-SHORAKAAA-EHIM IN KAANOO SAADEQEEN.\nDo they have any ‘partners’ [that they claim for Allah]? Then let them produce their partners, if they are truthful.\nيَوْمَ يُكْشَفُ عَن سَاقٍ وَيُدْعَوْنَ اِلَى السُّجُودِ فَلَا يَسْتَطِيعُونَ (42)\nYAWMA YUKSHAFO A’N SAAQINW WA YUD-A’WNA ELAS SOJOODE FALAA YASTATEE-O’ON.\nThe day when the catastrophe occurs and they are summoned to prostrate themselves, they will not be able [to do it].\nخٰشِعَةً اَبْصٰرُهُمْ تَرْهَقُهُمْ ذِلَّةٌ وَقَدْ كَانُوا۟ يُدْعَوْنَ اِلَى السُّجُودِ وَهُمْ سٰلِمُونَ (43)\nKHAASHE-A’TAN ABSAAROHUM TARHAQOHUM ZILLAH, WA QAD KAANOO YUD-A’WNA ELAS SOJOODE WA HUM SAALEMOON.\nWith a humbled look [in their eyes], they will be overcast by abasement. Certainly, they were summoned to prostrate themselves while they were yet sound.\nفَذَرْنِى وَمَن يُكَذِّبُ بِهٰذَا الْحَدِيثِ سَنَسْتَدْرِجُهُم مِّنْ حَيْثُ لَا يَعْلَمُونَ (44)\nFA-ZARNEE WA MAN-Y YOKAZZEBO BEHAAZAL HADEES, SANASTADREJOHUM MIN HAYSO LAA YA’LAMOON.\nSo leave Me with those who deny this discourse. We will draw them imperceptibly [into ruin], whence they do not know.\nوَاُمْلِى لَهُمْ اِنَّ كَيْدِى مَتِينٌ (45)\nWA UMLEE LAHUM, INNA KAYDEE MATEEN.\nI will grant them respite, for My devising is indeed sure.\nاَمْ تَسَْٔلُهُمْ اَجْرًا فَهُم مِّن مَّغْرَمٍ مُّثْقَلُونَ (46)\nAM TAS-ALOHUM AJRAN FAHUM MIM MAGHRAMIM MUSQALOON.\nDo you ask them for a reward, so that they are weighed down with debt?\nاَمْ عِندَهُمُ الْغَيْبُ فَهُمْ يَكْتُبُونَ (47)\nAM I’NDAHOMUL GHAYBO FAHUM YAKTOBOON.\nDo they possess [access to] the Unseen, so that they write it down?\nفَاصْبِرْ لِحُكْمِ رَبِّكَ وَلَا تَكُن كَصَاحِبِ الْحُوتِ اِذْ نَادَىٰ وَهُوَ مَكْظُومٌ (48)\nFASBIR LE-HUKME RABBEKA WA LAA TAKUN KASAAHEBIL HOOTE IZ NAADAA WA HOWA MAKZOOM.\nSo submit patiently to the judgement of your Lord, and do not be like the Man of the Fish who called out as he choked with grief.\nلَّوْلَآ اَن تَدٰرَكَهُۥ نِعْمَةٌ مِّن رَّبِّهِۦ لَنُبِذَ بِالْعَرَآءِ وَهُوَ مَذْمُومٌ (49)\nLAWLAA AN TADAARAKAHU NE’MATUM MIR RABBEHI LANOBEZA BIL-A’RAAA-E WA HOWA MAZMOOM.\nHad it not been for a blessing that came to his rescue from his Lord, he would surely have been cast on the bare shore, being blameworthy.\nفَاجْتَبٰهُ رَبُّهُۥ فَجَعَلَهُۥ مِنَ الصّٰلِحِينَ (50)\nFAJTABAAHO RABBOHU FA-JA-A’LAHU MENAS SAALEHEEN.\nSo his Lord chose him and made him one of the righteous.\nوَاِن يَكَادُ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟ لَيُزْلِقُونَكَ بِاَبْصٰرِهِمْ لَمَّا سَمِعُوا۟ الذِّكْرَ وَيَقُولُونَ اِنَّهُۥ لَمَجْنُونٌ (51)\nWA IN-Y YAKAADUL LAZEENA KAFAROO LAYUZLEQOONAKA BE-ABSAAREHIM LAMMAA SAME-U’Z ZIKRA WA YAQOOLOONA INNAHU LA-MAJNOON.\nIndeed the faithless almost devour you with their eyes when they hear this Reminder, and they say, ‘He is indeed crazy.’\nوَمَا هُوَ اِلَّا ذِكْرٌ لِّلْعٰلَمِينَ (52)\nWA MAA HOWA ILLAA ZIKRUL LIL-A’ALAMEEN.\nYet it is just a reminder for all the nations.",
  "merits": "There are 52 verses in this ‘Makki’ Surah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that the one who recites this Surah will never face financial difficulties. Writing this Surah and tying it to any part of the body that is suffering from pain alleviates the pain."
}
